Template: credentials/passphrase
Type: password
Description: Passphrase used to encrypt the credentials:
 This passphrase derives the key that encrypts the "credentials" column of
 the database. It is not stored in clear text: systemd-creds encrypts it
 with this machine's TPM2 chip and host key so the service can start on its
 own. Use at least 12 characters.
 .
 If a database already exists in /var/lib/credentials, enter the passphrase
 it was created with.
 .
 Leave empty to set it later with: sudo credentials-passphrase

Template: credentials/passphrase-again
Type: password
Description: Confirm the passphrase:

Template: credentials/passphrase-mismatch
Type: error
Description: Passphrases do not match
 The two entries are different. Please try again.

Template: credentials/passphrase-too-short
Type: error
Description: Passphrase too short
 The passphrase must be at least 12 characters long.
